; An @external var read only by the audio thread: its audience has no main
; bit, so embedder writes flow to audio directly through the table — the
; main thread must never adopt it (no main-adopt lines may appear). Main
; publishes it exactly once, at the entry bootstrap (the initializer, for
; the embedder's benefit); the start-audio bootstrap leaves it alone,
; since a snapshot already exists for the new audio replica to adopt.
@external
(var gain: f32 0.1)

@audio
(defn f [t: f32
         rate: f32]: f32
  gain)

@cpu
(defn main []
  (spawn-window (fn []
                    (start-audio f))))
